WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
Disney's latest movie Zootopia

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.389
has something for everyone!

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:08.940
Cute talking animals, a positive message
of social acceptance, crack cocaine! Truly

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.940
a movie for the whole family.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.940
MatPat Awesome Intro**

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:26.780
*Music

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:31.450
Hello Internet! Welcome to Film Theory.
The show that makes it slightly less

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.780
creepy that I'm sitting solo in a movie
theater, watching a Disney movie,

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.640
surrounded by screaming children. But
seriously, I love Disney movies. In a time

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.809
where the world is so full of fear, hate,
and Youtube rage comments, it's nice to visit

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:47.920
a bright colorful fantasy world where
things are simpler... happier...

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.480
Ahh who am I kidding? Disney movies are
dark. Bambi's mom dies,

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.551
Pinocchio gets kidnapped and sold into
slavery!

00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:57.250
𝘚𝘊𝘈𝘙 𝘎𝘌𝘛𝘚 𝘌𝘈𝘛𝘌𝘕 𝘈𝘓𝘐𝘝𝘌.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.330
But Zootopia may just be the darkest of the
bunch. If you haven't seen it,

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:06.460
you totally should. Right now, in fact. Not
only is it a fun movie, but, uh, this video is

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:10.360
just riddled with spoilers so consider
yourself warned. To get you up though

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.229
Zootopia tells the story of Judy Hopps.
An ambitious young rabbit who fulfills

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:17.619
her dream of becoming the first rabbit
police officer in the history of this

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:22.030
all-animal society. Here in Zootopia,
predators and prey co-exist peacefully,

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.840
but some predators have mysteriously
gone missing as of late and it's up to

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.460
Judy to crack the case.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.360
Not only is it a really fun detective
story, Zootopia also shined some light on

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.000
really important social issues, like how
goshdarn slow the DMV is!

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:36.500
(picture flash sound)

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:39.880
Gah!

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.890
Simultaneously hilarious, but

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:45.550
just downright depressing. But when you
look beyond its cute animals as humans

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:46.090
cover,

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:50.410
Zootopia is truly a story about race. The
idea of the minority group in society:

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:54.190
The Predators. Facing prejudice and
mistreatment from the majority is a

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:58.060
pretty thinly veiled allusion to
America's spotty history of race relations.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:01.899
Don't believe me? We see an ice cream
parlor refuse to serve a predator,

00:02:01.899 --> 00:02:05.350
police being quicker to draw weapons
against predators, and even Judy

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:10.160
hypothesizes that predators are
biologically more savage than prey.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.640
Man, those are some heavy themes! I feel
bad for those parents who made the

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.810
"responsible choice"

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:18.590
to take their kids to Zootopia instead of
Deadpool! A good idea but now I have to

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:22.460
try and explain eugenics to a
four-year-old. But while the "Zootopia is

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:26.810
about racism" concept may not be
surprising to an astute viewer, it goes even

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.190
deeper than that. Because this children's
movie about a rabbit who just wants to

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:35.450
be a cop is actually a retelling of a
long-standing conspiracy theory that

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.690
crack cocaine was devised to destroy black communities in America!

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.200
Bet you didn't see that one coming.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:43.100
Whoa-ho, time out MatPat!

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.420
You, the skeptical viewer (HEY DID YOU CALL ME A DOG HOW DARE YOU)

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:48.200
are probably shouting "Disney may go dark, but
they don't go THAT dark!" (OR DO THEY)

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.580
Hey, I understand your skepticism but
Disney is no stranger to drug use.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.640
Remember when Dumbo drinks some water
that has champagne in it and gets so

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.700
wasted that he hallucinates pink
elephants and wakes up hungover in a

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.270
tree? Or when Alice from Alice in
Wonderland eats some special mushrooms

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:05.840
that make her perceptions of reality
change? And when it comes to drugs there's

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.350
even a Breaking Bad joke in the movie!
And if you want to see how dark Disney

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.420
is willing to go,

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.870
did you watch Maleficent? If you did you
probably understand that that was pretty

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.150
much a fairy tale retelling of the story
of a rape survivor!

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:21.350
Yeah, Disney makes fun animated movies
that are for kids, but they sure aren't

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:24.500
afraid to tackle some pretty intense
stuff for the benefit of the adults in

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.280
the audience.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:30.290
So, why not crack cocaine? And by that I
mean why would they not talk about crack

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.370
cocaine and not

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:35.480
why should we all do crack cocaine  (Oh). Crack 
is wack kids (Hey copying me I see)! Just say no! Other

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:39.590
Reagan-era slogans. Now obviously the
movie's characters don't smoke actual

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:43.430
crack, but Zootopia has its own substance
called Night Howler. And the similarities

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:47.540
between crack and Night Howlers are
pretty surprising! One last reminder that

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.200
it's about to strike Spoiler o'clock, so
if you're afraid of turning back into a

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.990
pumpkin it's time to

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:58.480
run away from the ball now. The ball
being this video... That metaphor just

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.430
spun wildly out of control.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:05.230
Spoilers ahead, let's go. Evidence number
one: Night Howler serum and crack are

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:09.100
both synthesized from harmless plants.
As we see in Zootopia, Night Howlers

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.120
are flowers that grow wild on Judy's
parents' carrot farm. Nobody had any idea

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.500
that they were key to some psychotropic
drug, until a fox tells them so. Even

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.770
after they've been harvested, Judy
mistakes the bulbs for onions when she

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:24.460
stops a weasel who's stealing them to
turn them into Night Howler serum.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:28.390
Similarly, if you took Crack Cocaine back
to its most basic form, you'd probably

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.730
walk right on past it without another
thought.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:34.690
Crack, and Cocaine in general, comes from
the leaves of the Coca plant, which is

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.180
indigenous to much of South and Central America.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:41.050
Raw Coca is so harmless that most people
make it into tea, or put it into

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:45.310
habit-forming sodas back in the day. But
concentrating coca extract from several

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.960
pounds of leaves results in a few grams
of pure Colombian nose candy.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.990
Of course then you have to chemically
treat the powder version of Cocaine and

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.500
cook it to turn it into Crack, so there
is a lot of lab work that goes into

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.490
turning leaves into crack. And in
Zootopia we get a good look at the

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:04.330
complicated chemistry lab used to
produce Night Howler serum by Doug the

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.650
sheep and his partners.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:08.650
Given the variety and sophistication of
equipment we see in the lab it's

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:12.820
reasonable to conclude that synthesizing
Night Howler serum and crack cocaine are

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:17.320
similar processes. But this leads to one
question: why crack and not something

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.310
like, say, crystal meth? I mean again,
there's a breaking bad reference in the

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:22.300
scene after all.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:26.290
Well, here's the thing: crystal meth isn't
made from living plant matter.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:27.910
Meth's active ingredients are

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:31.940
usually synthesized from chemical sources,
like cough medicine. Besides we all know

00:05:31.959 --> 00:05:35.739
that the only use Walter White has for
flowers is poisoning innocent children.

00:05:35.739 --> 00:05:39.129
Hoho, isn't this a happy episode?
Can't wait for this one to get suggested

00:05:39.129 --> 00:05:41.559
against all those disney toy unboxing
videos.

00:05:41.559 --> 00:05:46.689
Anyway let's cheer things up a bit.
Here's a cute picture of a sloth. Aww, he's such a cutesie! [MatPat pls control yourself]

00:05:46.689 --> 00:05:47.949
Oh ho ho, lookit dis guy! [MatPat back to crack pls]

00:05:47.949 --> 00:05:51.549
Alright, back to crack. Evidence number
two: Night Howlers and crack cocaine

00:05:51.549 --> 00:05:53.679
effect user in the same way.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.480
While Zootopia doesn't tell us a whole
lot about what it's like to be on Night

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.940
Howler serum, we can get some clues by
observing those who are under its

00:05:59.949 --> 00:06:03.279
influence. Emmitt Otterton scratches up
the entire back seat of his limousine,

00:06:03.279 --> 00:06:07.329
rambles incoherently about the night
howlers and then attacks his driver for

00:06:07.329 --> 00:06:10.689
no reason. When Judy goes to question the
driver, we see that the night howlers

00:06:10.689 --> 00:06:13.959
affect animals almost instantly as one
second they're having a pleasant

00:06:13.959 --> 00:06:17.829
conversation and the next he goes
full-on rage virus on her. So Night

00:06:17.829 --> 00:06:21.879
Howler effects include mania, incoherence and near-instant aggression.

00:06:21.879 --> 00:06:23.199
How does this compare with crack?

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:27.399
Speaking from personal experience, I... have
no idea. No experience in the drug realm.

00:06:27.399 --> 00:06:30.909
Trust me, we go to some pretty crazy
lengths to research these episodes but

00:06:30.909 --> 00:06:32.800
uh... not that far.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.369
I'm not passing out crack pipes in the
Edit room and taking notes.

00:06:36.369 --> 00:06:40.149
However a butt ton of internet research
shows that it matches up pretty well.

00:06:40.149 --> 00:06:44.259
Effects of smoking crack include
restlessness, anxiety, irritability, and in

00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:48.429
large doses, aggression, paranoia and
delusions. Running through walls, however...

00:06:48.429 --> 00:06:49.929
not on that list. Sorry, Dave.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.899
As for how fast you feel the
effects of crack after you've smoked it, it's

00:06:52.899 --> 00:06:56.979
hard to locate an exact number but
smoking the drug is the fastest way to

00:06:56.979 --> 00:06:59.769
get it into your bloodstream outside of
injecting it, and some of the most

00:06:59.769 --> 00:07:03.519
official sounding people on the internet
talking about crack claim that it works

00:07:03.519 --> 00:07:04.839
almost instantly.

00:07:04.839 --> 00:07:07.650
Obviously the drugs aren't meant to be
exactly the same -

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:11.880
this is an allegory after all - but based
on their effects they might as well be.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:16.350
Evidence number three: Night Howlers and
crack affect the same groups.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:19.740
Zootopia makes a point to make sure that
we know that predators are the minority,

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.990
and that predators are the only ones

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:26.130
quote unquote "going savage" as a result
of the Night Howler serum.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.630
While the movie doesn't explicitly tell
us which minority predators are,

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:33.380
it's pretty clear that we're talking about
African-Americans. I alluded to it before

00:07:33.389 --> 00:07:38.130
but we see Nick Wilde the fox denied
service at an ice cream parlor simply

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:41.610
because he's a predator, and the tension
between Zootopia's police force and

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.970
predators is a transparent allusion to
the issues brought up in the

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:49.320
#BlackLivesMatter movement. Also
Assistant Mayor Bellwether tells us that

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:53.160
Zootopia's population is ten percent
predator: a very similar mark to the

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:57.020
twelve point three percent of the U.S.
population that's African-American.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:01.320
The Predators are also all disappearing from
Zootopia's Precinct 1, which is referred

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:05.070
to as the city center when Judy is
assigned to it at her graduation from the

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:06.000
police academy.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.270
All of this mirrors the group that was
hit hardest by crack cocaine in the

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.130
1980s: inner-city
African-Americans.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.550
A paper by future freakonomics Steven Levitt

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:18.720
stated that the incidence
of crack usage per capita was ten times

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:23.310
as high in large cities with low-income
urban populations such as New York,

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:28.320
Philadelphia and Washington DC. Crack
also affected black communities really

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.440
disproportionately, as during the crack
boom of the eighties and early nineties,

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:36.690
eighty-five percent of arrests made
related to crack were of African-Americans.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:40.080
But I'm sure some of you are probably still
skeptical. Sure Night Howlers make you

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:44.180
act like you're on crack, affected
minority communities and come from plants.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:47.800
So what? In this movie there's a big
government conspiracy around the Night Howlers.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:51.120
Assistant Mayor Bellwether is
the one behind the drug getting spread,

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:54.959
developing a serum that her minions
administered to predators via dart gun.

00:08:54.959 --> 00:08:58.560
She admits that she began the conspiracy
to ensure that the prey majority could

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:01.480
keep the peace by making everyone afraid
of predators.

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:04.380
As she puts it, fear always works.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.589
But it's not like in real life there was
some big government conspiracy to

00:09:07.589 --> 00:09:12.270
provide african americans with crack out
of paranoia for national safety, right?

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:19.940
Right?? WELL, evidence number four: Night
Howlers and crack are both government conspiracies.

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:22.620
There are some OG theorists
out there who believe that the crack

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.860
cocaine epidemic back in the nineteen
eighties came from a similar kind of

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:29.970
government conspiracy, as that showed in
Zootopia. Before we go on let me take a

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:30.990
minute to get serious.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:35.339
I should mention that this is a really
controversial theory and not one to take lightly.

00:09:35.339 --> 00:09:39.120
If you're interested in any of this, do
some research and reading for yourself.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:42.750
There's no way that in the final minutes
of my video on Zootopia that i can give

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:46.440
this topic the true depth and explanation
that it deserves. It's my goal with this

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:49.860
show to just inspire you guys, to learn
more about the world around you,

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.700
and not always take new stories at face value.

00:09:52.709 --> 00:09:56.970
Anyway, regardless of the truth of this
theory, it reeks of the events depicted

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:01.800
in Zootopia. In 1996, a San José journalist
named Gary Webb wrote a three-part

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:05.790
report called Dark Alliance, which
exposed a complicated web of connections

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.850
between the American government and the
spread of crack cocaine in the

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:12.570
predominantly African-American
neighborhood of South Los Angeles.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.560
Like I've already said it's a really
complicated story that i won't get too

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:20.620
deep into here, but basically America,
afraid of the spread of communism during the Cold War,

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.900
supported a "gorilla" [lol]
resistance group known as the Contras.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.490
Not those gorillas, guerrilla.

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:29.670
Though it's an easy mistake considering that
this is Zootopia... You know what, nevermind.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:33.300
Just use gorillas, use the gorillas. And
no, the Contras is not referring to the

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:37.170
old NES game. Anyway this support in the
Contras resulted in the CIA becoming

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:39.230
involved with a bunch of drug smugglers.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.860
And this is a hundred percent true a
Senate report confirmed that the drug

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:45.560
traffickers had been provided with
federal money.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.920
Once the funding for the Contras ran out,
they were given the green light to raise

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:52.900
money for themselves. And how do you do
that if you're a small Central American country?

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.300
Lemonade stands? Bake sales?

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:58.450
Nope! Drugs. They flooded the west coast
with cheap cocaine,

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:00.520
while the government willingly looked the other way -

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:05.540
or, as some speculate, provided planes to
aid in the shipment of the narcotics between countries.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:09.800
By 1987 crack was ravaging practically
all of America's large cities,

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:14.260
hitting low-income black neighborhoods the
hardest. The dealer who started it all?

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:18.050
A man by the name of Ricky Ross believes
that spreading cracked african-americans

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:21.680
was a conscious choice by the government;
one that then President Ronald Reagan

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.220
made out of a desire to keep the country
safe from the Soviet Union and the

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:29.180
spread of communism. Ross has said, quote: "I
believe that they felt it was more

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:33.940
valuable to sacrifice a particular
sector of America, and a race of people in America,

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:37.020
in order to save the whole
country" end quote.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:41.260
It's an idea that Mayor Lionheart echoes towards the end
of Zootopia, saying that they did

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:45.250
quote: "The wrong thing for the right
reasons" end quote.

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:48.500
Zootopia even seems like it's
making references to specific instances

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:52.220
of the crack epidemic. In the movie Mayor
Lionheart gets set up to make it look

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.420
like he's behind the Night Howler scheme
and gets put in jail -

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:58.160
only to return to power after his release.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:02.870
It's awfully similar to Washington DC
Mayor Marion Barry who was caught

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:08.240
smoking crack, jailed and then reelected
as mayor when he was released from prison.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.840
Stay classy, DC. Long story short, the
level of government involvement with the

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:15.620
spread of crack in America is still in
question, but if I ever go missing know

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:19.220
it was the government silencing me for
this video. Or the one where I researched

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:22.940
atomic bombs and Batman. Or my old
Polybius video back on Game Theory.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.680
Man I've got to be on so many watch
lists at this point. [They gon' get you, MatPat.]

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.140
Anyway, there you have it.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:30.440
Zootopia: educating our
children about a government conspiracy

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:34.360
to spread an organic rage drug to
inner-city minority groups.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:37.790
Kinda makes you yearn for the simpler days
of princesses with Stockholm Syndrome.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.790
But hey, that's just a theory -

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:48.500
a depressing theory - and a conspiracy
theory! But most of all, a Film Theory!

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.420
Aaaaaand... cut!

